{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_classical_bridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_ns_classical_bridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.enstrophy_alpha_one_of_dissipation_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.enstrophy_alpha_one_of_dissipation_closure","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L119-L142","doc":"**Critical-exponent closure α = 1 (dissipation closure).**\n\nUnder the standard turbulence closure `ε = ν_q · Ω` (mean dissipation =\nq-viscosity × enstrophy) with `ν_q = (q − 1)/(2q)`, the enstrophy order\nparameter satisfies the exact identity\n\n`Ω · (q − 1) = 2 q ε`.\n\nAs `q → 1⁺` with `ε` bounded away from `0`, the right side tends to `2ε > 0`\nwhile `q − 1 → 0`, so `Ω ~ (q − 1)^{−1}`: the critical exponent is\n**α = 1**, conditional on this closure and on `ε ↛ 0`.  The corpus's\ncompeting `α = 4/3` follows from a *different* closure (a Kolmogorov\n`k^{−5/3}` spectrum truncated at `N_eff`); the two are not reconciled — see\nthe audit, Finding 2.  The `2q ≠ 0` hypothesis is the only ring condition\nthe identity needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.obstruction_zero_of_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.obstruction_zero_of_regular","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**Contrapositive: global regularity forces a vanishing obstruction —\nCONDITIONAL on Bridge (B).**  A sanity check that the bridge criterion is\nused in the honest direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.classical_blowup_of_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.classical_blowup_of_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L93-L108","doc":"**Internal blow-up transfers from a non-vanishing obstruction — CONDITIONAL\non Bridge (B).**\n\nGiven `NS_A ≠ 0`, the QOU's internal `q = 1` flow blows up.  *Derived* from\nthe bridge criterion (`NS_A = 0 ↔ globallyRegular`) and the internal blow-up\ndichotomy (`blowsUp ↔ ¬ globallyRegular`) — not asserted.  The instance\n`[CategoricalClassicalNSBridge NS_A]` is the **open wall**; this theorem\nshows only that the (unconditional) categorical side transfers to the\n*QOU-internal* flow *given* the bridge.  It says nothing about the external\n`ℝ³` PDE and does not resolve the Clay problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.obstruction_is_regularity_criterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.obstruction_is_regularity_criterion","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**B1 (the bridge criterion).** The categorical obstruction is a faithful\nregularity criterion for the QOU-internal flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.blowup_iff_not_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.blowup_iff_not_regular","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Internal blow-up ⟺ failure of internal global regularity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.blowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.blowsUp","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Finite-time singularity of the QOU's internal `q = 1` NS flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.globallyRegular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.globallyRegular","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Global regularity of the QOU's internal `q = 1` NS flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CategoricalClassicalNSBridge","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_ns_classical_bridge.lean#L65-L91","doc":"**Bridge (B): the obstruction ↔ internal-flow transfer, given a QOU.**\n`@conjecture: primary` — an *open* conjecture, axiomatised as a\ncontent-bearing class with **no instance**.\n\nFields are the bridge *hypotheses*, never its conclusion (§3b-cond cond. 5,\nnon-degenerate):\n\n* `globallyRegular` / `blowsUp` — the two states of the **QOU's own internal\n  `q = 1` flow** (`ns-obstruction-tower`), NOT the classical `ℝ³` PDE. The\n  identification of this internal flow with the external PDE is the separate\n  open hypothesis B2 (see the module docstring) and is not encoded here.\n* `blowup_iff_not_regular` — internal blow-up is exactly the failure of\n  internal global regularity (a BKM-type dichotomy for the internal flow).\n* `obstruction_is_regularity_criterion` — **B1, the transfer statement**:\n  the categorical obstruction is a *faithful* regularity criterion for the\n  QOU-internal flow, i.e. it vanishes iff that flow is globally regular. ","signatureChunk":0}]}